# Origin: legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/class.chk
# Milestone: M6 Wave 3 (Phase 3 — Gap #2 multi-slot class body)
#
# The legacy fixture tests S-class-name-scope: the name of the class
# being defined is not available during parsing of its proto list.  As a
# consequence, `class a : public a { ... }` resolves the proto `a` to the
# OUTER `a`.
#
# The original fixture wraps everything in `{ ... }` bare blocks which
# are not legal as top-level statements in v1.0 line-oriented REPL;
# adapted here with same-line shadow chaining (identical semantics, see
# tests/chk/objects/class.chk for the primary port).
#
# Wave 3 extension: extends the port with multi-slot class bodies
# (Gap #2) which were blocked before this wave.

# Core S-class-name-scope semantic (port of original single test case).
class a { var foo = 40 }; class a : public a { var bar = 2 }; var b = a.new(); b.foo + b.bar
[00000000] 42

# Wave 3 extension: multi-slot class body with shadow scoping.
class Base { var x = 1; var y = 2 }; class Child : public Base { var z = 3 }; var c = Child.new(); c.x + c.y + c.z
[00000001] 6

